I walk further through the large shop.
I still need something for my ears.
Because the cold wind outside is bad.
Then I see a small table with winter clothes.
Many thick wool hats are lying there.
I like two hats.
I see a yellow hat and a grey hat.
Which one do I take, the yellow one or the grey one?
I briefly put down the green coat and the grey sweatshirt.
Then I put on the yellow hat.
It is warm and very soft.
I look in the mirror.
The yellow hat and the green coat go super together.
I look for the price tag.
The beautiful hat costs only fifteen euros.
That is cheap, but the quality is good.
So I take the thick coat, the comfortable sweatshirt, and the new hat.
Now I am going to the till, because I would like to pay.
